# Redirects from the Webflow site this replaced.
#
# Derived from Webflow's own sitemap (18 published URLs) by
# scripts/audit-urls.mjs, then checked by hand. Re-run that workflow if the
# live site changes before cutover.
#
# 301, not 302: these moves are permanent. A 302 asks crawlers to keep the OLD
# URL as canonical, which is the opposite of the point - the whole reason this
# file exists is to pass the old pages' ranking and inbound links on to the new
# ones. Without it every case study and post 404s the moment DNS moves.
#
# Not listed, because they are already identical on both sites: /, /about,
# /blog, /collage, /merchfolio, /portfolio, /privacy-policy, /video,
# /image-license-info and /work/hug-a-mug.

# Case studies. Webflow served these under /case-studies/; this site uses
# /work/. Every one moves even where the slug is unchanged.
/case-studies/adelante-barbell-club                    /work/adelante-barbell-club   301
/case-studies/dumpstat-podcast                         /work/dumpstat                301
/case-studies/hug-a-mug-coffeehouse-ceramics-studio    /work/hug-a-mug               301

# Blog. Webflow served posts under /post/; this site uses /blog/.
/post/brand-identity-cost-why-400-is-too-low   /blog/brand-identity-cost-why-400-is-too-low   301
/post/logo-design-worth-paying-for             /blog/logo-design-worth-paying-for             301

# Published Webflow leftovers, deliberately not ported: two abandoned duplicate
# drafts and an unused collection template. Sent somewhere sensible rather than
# left to 404, since they may still be indexed or linked.
/home2026                            /              301
/portfolio-copy-3                    /portfolio     301
